```

**Fire**:
```js
function fireWeapon(spec) {
  if (state.time < state.nextFire) return;
  const action = spec.action_behavior;
  state.nextFire = state.time + action.cooldown;
  state.cooldownTotal = action.cooldown;
  state.aimingUntil = state.time + 1.1;
  state.recoil = 1;
  AudioFX.shoot(); buzz(9);
  const dir = camera.getWorldDirection(new THREE.Vector3()).normalize();
  const origin = new THREE.Vector3(playerBody.position.x, playerBody.position.y + 0.9, playerBody.position.z).add(dir.clone().multiplyScalar(0.75));
  // hand-ish offset
  const right = new THREE.Vector3(1,0,0).applyAxisAngle(UP, playerGroup.rotation.y);
  origin.add(right.multiplyScalar(0.3));
  const visuals = spec.projectile_visuals && spec.projectile_visuals.length ? spec.projectile_visuals : defaultProjectileVisuals(spec);
  for (let i=0;i<action.spawnCount;i++){
    const spread = action.spread;
    const d = dir.clone().add(new THREE.Vector3(rand(-spread,spread), rand(-spread,spread), rand(-spread,spread))).normalize();
    const pos = origin.clone().add(new THREE.Vector3(rand(-.05,.05), rand(-.05,.05), rand(-.05,.05)));
    spawnEntity(spec, {
      position: pos,
      velocity: d.multiplyScalar(action.speed),
      isProjectile: true,
      visuals,
      action,
      life: 8,
      scale: action.projectileScale,
      onImpact: action.onImpact,
    });
  }
  muzzleFlash(origin.clone().add(dir.clone().multiplyScalar(0.3)), "#ffe0a0");
  dom.reticle.classList.remove("pulse");
  void dom.reticle.offsetWidth;
  dom.reticle.classList.add("pulse");
  // cooldown UI
  dom.useBtn.style.setProperty("--cd", "0");
  dom.useBtn.classList.remove("ready");
}
```
Potential issue: `camera.getWorldDirection` returns direction camera is looking; good. But third-person camera looks slightly down at player, so firing direction points down. We want more horizontal. Use `dir.y += 0.08` and normalize? The camera target is player chest; camera above and behind, so direction points slightly downward. Aim at where camera looks: down. For shooting, better to aim along camera forward but add 0.12 up. Also since origin at chest, and camera looks at chest, direction from camera to target is down; projectiles go into ground. Need a proper aim ray. Compute camera forward, then `aimPoint = camera.position + forward*40`; direction = (aimPoint - origin).normalize(). This still points from camera to 40m ahead along its view; since camera looks at player chest, at 40m the ray is near ground? The camera is at y~3.5 looking at chest y~1.35, downward slope ~2/6.7 = 0.3; at 40m it's way below ground. Hmm.

Better: aim direction should be horizontal with slight downward/upward based on camera pitch. Use camera yaw for horizontal and a fixed slight upward angle:
```js
const dir = new THREE.Vector3(-Math.sin(cam.yaw), 0.02 - cam.pitch*0.15, -Math.cos(cam.yaw)).normalize();
```
